@startuml

title The material each action kind reads from the job's payload

class "execute_sql" as sql <<action kind>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +statement : text
}

class "send_mq_message" as mq <<action kind>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +queue : queue id
    {field} +message type : name
    {field} +body : text
}

class "nats_publish" as pub <<action kind>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +subject : subject name
    {field} +receiver : name, or none
    {field} +tenant : tenant id, or none
}

note bottom of sql
    The statement runs as the scheduler's
    own database identity, so its reach is
    a question of permission.
end note

note bottom of mq
    The scheduler owns the handover;
    the queue owns the delivery.
end note

note bottom of pub
    A subject with no receiver is a notification:
    the scheduler publishes and reads no reply.
    A named receiver makes the publication a
    request, and a refusal fails the firing.
end note

@enduml
